@startuml power-domains
' LocalAiRobot — DETAILED power + signal wiring (camera, face & 3-sensor array).
' This source lives next to its render. Regenerate in place (writes power-domains.png here):
'   plantuml -tpng docs/images/power-domains.puml
' No Graphviz needed: !pragma layout smetana uses PlantUML's pure-Java layout engine.
' ONE 3S LiPo now feeds everything: an ESC branch (drive + servo BEC) and a UBEC->UPS branch for the Pi.
!pragma layout smetana
hide stereotype
title LocalAiRobot — power from ONE 3S LiPo (UBEC->UPS->Pi + ESC->drive) + sensors, camera & face

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 12
  FontSize 12
  BorderThickness 1
  BackgroundColor<<io>> #DAE8FC
  BorderColor<<io>> #6C8EBF
  BackgroundColor<<model>> #FFF2CC
  BorderColor<<model>> #D6B656
  BackgroundColor<<data>> #D5E8D4
  BorderColor<<data>> #82B366
  BackgroundColor<<motor>> #F8CECC
  BorderColor<<motor>> #B85450
  BackgroundColor<<store>> #F5F5F5
  BorderColor<<store>> #666666
  BackgroundColor<<motordomain>> #FBEAEA
  BorderColor<<motordomain>> #B85450
  BackgroundColor<<braindomain>> #E6EEF8
  BorderColor<<braindomain>> #6C8EBF
}

' ---- brain rail: Pi power + everything the Pi drives directly ----
rectangle "Brain rail  (UBEC -> UPS HAT -> Pi)" as brainbox <<braindomain>> {
  rectangle "UPS HAT (2x 18650 = backup)\nfed by the UBEC (or 27W PSU on bench)" as ups <<io>>
  rectangle "Raspberry Pi 5\n+ Active Cooler (mandatory)" as pi <<io>>
  rectangle "HC-SR04P x3  (3.3V; no divider)\nfront 23/24  •  left 5/6  •  right 20/21" as sonar <<data>>
  rectangle "Camera: Arducam IMX519\n(16MP autofocus, CSI via 22->15 adapter)" as cam <<data>>
  rectangle "Face screen\n(USB-C -> /dev/ttyACM0)" as face <<io>>
}
ups --> pi : 5V to Pi
pi --> sonar : 3.3V + TRIG/ECHO
pi --> cam : CSI ribbon
pi --> face : USB-C (serial)

' ---- ONE 3S LiPo source: a high-current ESC branch AND a UBEC step-down branch feeding the Pi ----
rectangle "Power  (single 3S LiPo source)" as motorbox <<motordomain>> {
  rectangle "3S 11.1V LiPo" as lipo <<motor>>
  rectangle "ESC\n(battery input + BEC for servo)" as esc <<motor>>
  rectangle "drive motor" as dmotor <<motor>>
  rectangle "steering servo\n(DS3225 HV, on the ESC BEC rail)" as servo <<motor>>
}
rectangle "ZTW UBEC step-down\n(3S in -> 5-6V/6A out, jumper-set)" as ubec <<motor>>
lipo --> esc  : 11.1 V (high current)
lipo --> ubec : 11.1 V (tap)
ubec --> ups  : 5-6 V -> UPS input
esc --> dmotor : motor drive

' ---- 3.3V logic/PWM signals + the servo's BEC rail + common GND ----
rectangle "PCA9685\n(I2C PWM bridge, 0x40)" as pca <<model>>
rectangle "common GND bus\n(Pi <-> PCA9685 <-> ESC <-> UBEC)" as gnd <<store>>

pi  --> pca   : 3.3V logic (VCC) + I2C SDA/SCL
esc --> pca   : ch0 throttle PWM (signal)
esc --> pca   : BEC -> V+ rail (servo power)
pca --> servo : ch1: BEC V+ + PWM

esc  ..> gnd : GND
pi   ..> gnd : GND
pca  ..> gnd : GND
ubec ..> gnd : GND

note bottom of gnd
  **ONE 3S LiPo powers everything** via two branches: the **ESC** (drive motor + BEC for the servo/V+ rail)
  and the **UBEC (5-6V) -> UPS input -> Pi**. The UPS 18650s stay as a **backup buffer** + clean shutdown.
  All parts share a **common GND**. The **ESC BEC -> PCA9685 V+ rail** is the servo's power (NOT the Pi's).
  **Servo: use an HV (7.4V) servo, or feed V+ from a separate 5-6V BEC** (a 6V-only servo can be damaged).
  Set the UBEC jumper to the UPS's rated input (typically 5V). DS3225 stall ~2.5-3A — if the ESC BEC browns
  out under hard steering, add a separate servo BEC on V+. All 3 HC-SR04**P** are 3.3V (ECHO Pi-safe).
end note
@enduml
